{# The weekly digest as a script to be read aloud.

   Same whitespace convention as digest.md.j2: lone plain {% %} tags only.

   This is a sibling of that template, not a variant of it. What survives being
   spoken is a different set from what reads well on a page: no scores (a
   listener cannot compare "eight out of ten" to anything), no links, no
   interests-matched line, no basis label, no entity list, and none of the
   audit material at all — `maybe_interesting` is a bullet list and
   `everything_else` is a table, and both are unlistenable by construction.

   Blank lines are the pause cues, so they are load-bearing here in a way they
   are not in prose. Every value passes through `| speech`, which strips the
   Markdown a synthesiser would otherwise pronounce character by character. #}
Podcast digest for week {{ week_number }}, {{ year }}. {{ stats.summarized }} episode{{ '' if stats.summarized == 1 else 's' }} summarised out of {{ stats.scanned }} scanned.

